Some forward locations remain restricted despite the NACS agreement, yet the overall change still lets Tesla owners see real-time occupancy before they arrive.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:48.180
That small visibility upgrade matters most on long weekends or holiday travel days,

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:53.160
when drivers need to decide whether to stop at a particular site or push to the next one.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:05:01.000
All of this infrastructure and sourcing activity feeds into a larger question about where Tesla actually builds vehicles for different markets.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:11.480
The quick arrival of the Shanghai Model 3s in Canada shows that established production lines running at scale can move finished vehicles to an adjacent market in days,

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:18.400
